This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. **Primary Request and Intent:**

   The user's sole substantive request: **"can you replicate the web app in the react native app"**

   Because the web app is ~30k+ lines across 17 pages and 80+ components while mobile was ~2.4k lines, I asked three scoping questions via AskUserQuestion. The user answered:
   - **Scope (multi-select, chose ALL FOUR):** "Core chat parity" (streaming, stop/retry, model selector, persona-composed system prompt, auto-titling, session recovery), "Interactive learning cards" (quiz/question/goal/flashcard renderers with tag-parsing + result-feedback loop), "Settings + learner profile" (providers/models tab, teacher persona editor, UI settings, learner profile & insights), "Artifacts & sharing" (artifact viewer/browser, export/import, shared-session links, markdown+code rendering).
   - **Code sharing:** **"Copy into mobile/src"** — the user explicitly rejected my recommended "Extract to shared/" option. Mobile duplicates web logic rather than importing from `shared/`.
   - **Depth:** **"Build the highest-value slice now"** — implement the biggest single win end-to-end with tests, then iterate.

   I selected **streaming chat + the editable teacher persona** as the highest-value slice, since mobile was blocking-request-only (the most visible gap) and the persona/protocol split is the web's core identity architecture.

2. **Key Technical Concepts:**
   - Expo SDK 56 / React Native 0.85.3 / expo-router / React 19.2.3 / Metro bundler / Hermes
   - `expo/fetch` — Expo's winter-spec fetch that exposes a real `response.body` ReadableStream; React Native's built-in `fetch` (whatwg-fetch over XMLHttpRequest) does NOT expose a readable body, so streaming is impossible without it
   - `@earendil-works/pi-ai` — the web app's streaming library; **cannot run under Metro**, hence mobile needs a hand-rolled SSE implementation
   - Server-Sent Events (SSE) parsing with chunk-boundary buffering across three wire formats: OpenAI-compatible (`choices[0].delta.content`), Anthropic (`content_block_delta` → `delta.text`, requires `stream: true` + `anthropic-version: 2023-06-01`), Gemini (`:streamGenerateContent?alt=sse` → `candidates[0].content.parts[].text`)
   - Persona/protocol split: editable WHO (voice/values) vs. fixed HOW (pedagogy), composed per request so persona edits can't remove the teaching loop
   - Throttled React state flushes (60ms cadence) so token streams don't thrash FlatList re-renders
   - AsyncStorage (sessions/artifacts/persona) vs. Expo SecureStore + Android Keystore (API keys) privacy boundary
   - `bun test` for mobile tests (not vitest, not jest); bun's `Response` always exposes a body, unlike RN
   - Modules feeding testable layers must stay RN-import-free (AsyncStorage cannot be imported under `bun test`)

3. **Files and Code Sections:**

   - **`mobile/src/lib/persona.ts`** (CREATED)
     - Copies the web's `DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA` (John Keating, Dead Poets Society) verbatim from `web/src/keating/persona.ts`. Deliberately RN-import-free so `system-prompt.ts` → `provider-client.ts` stays testable under `bun test`.
     ```ts
     /**
      * Teacher persona — the editable identity/voice of the tutor.
      * ...
      * This module stays free of React Native imports so the prompt layer it feeds
      * can be exercised under plain `bun test`; persistence lives in
      * persona-storage.ts.
      */
     export const DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA = `You are John Keating, the English teacher from Dead Poets Society — reborn here as a hyperteacher for any subject a learner brings you.
     ... (Core principles 1-5: Diagnosis First, Reconstruction Over Regurgitation, Transfer Testing, Voice Preservation, Socratic Patience) ...
     Your role is to ensure every learner is equipped to contribute their own verse. O Captain, my Captain — but the ship is theirs to steer.`;

     export function normalizePersona(raw: unknown): string {
       if (typeof raw !== "string") return DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA;
       return raw.trim().length > 0 ? raw : DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA;
     }

     /** True when the stored persona is the untouched John Keating default. */
     export function isDefaultPersona(text: string): boolean {
       return text.trim() === DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA.trim();
     }
     ```

   - **`mobile/src/lib/persona-storage.ts`** (CREATED)
     - Isolates AsyncStorage so `persona.ts` remains test-importable.
     ```ts
     import AsyncStorage from "@react-native-async-storage/async-storage";
     import { DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA, normalizePersona } from "./persona";

     const PERSONA_STORAGE_KEY = "keating.mobile.teacher-persona";

     export async function loadPersona(): Promise<string> {
       try {
         return normalizePersona(await AsyncStorage.getItem(PERSONA_STORAGE_KEY));
       } catch (error) {
         console.warn("Failed to load teacher persona:", error);
         return DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA;
       }
     }
     export async function savePersona(text: string): Promise<void> {
       await AsyncStorage.setItem(PERSONA_STORAGE_KEY, normalizePersona(text));
     }
     export async function resetPersona(): Promise<void> {
       await AsyncStorage.removeItem(PERSONA_STORAGE_KEY);
     }
     ```

   - **`mobile/src/lib/system-prompt.ts`** (REWRITTEN — was a single hardcoded `KEATING_MOBILE_SYSTEM_PROMPT` string)
     - Now mirrors web's persona/protocol split. Paragraph 1 of the old prompt (identity) became the persona; paragraphs 2-4 (operational) became the fixed protocol.
     ```ts
     import { DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA, normalizePersona } from "./persona";

     export const KEATING_TEACHING_PROTOCOL = `Teach for mastery rather than surface agreement. Keep the learner active through a loop of diagnosis, intuition, formal core, misconception repair, worked example, retrieval, and reflection. ...

     Adapt to the domain. For mathematics, reach the formalism. ...

     Use clear Markdown that reads well on a phone. ...`;

     /** Composes the editable persona with the fixed protocol. */
     export function composeSystemPrompt(persona: string = DEFAULT_TEACHER_PERSONA): string {
       return `${normalizePersona(persona).trim()}\n\n${KEATING_TEACHING_PROTOCOL}`;
     }

     /** Default composition, used before a stored persona has loaded. */
     export const KEATING_MOBILE_SYSTEM_PROMPT = composeSystemPrompt();
     ```

   - **`mobile/src/lib/provider-client.ts`** (HEAVILY EXTENDED — the core of this slice)
     - `buildProviderRequest` signature changed from `(settings, apiKey, messages, signal?)` to `(settings, apiKey, messages, options: ProviderRequestOptions = {})` where options is `{ signal?, stream?, systemPrompt? }`. Existing tests called it with 3 args so they still pass.
     ```ts
     export interface ProviderRequestOptions {
       signal?: AbortSignal;
       /** Ask the provider for a Server-Sent Events token stream. */
       stream?: boolean;
       /** Composed persona + teaching protocol. Defaults to the built-in prompt. */
       systemPrompt?: string;
     }
     ```
     - Per-provider stream handling inside `buildProviderRequest`: `if (stream) commonHeaders.Accept = "text/event-stream";`; Anthropic/OpenAI bodies get `...(stream ? { stream: true } : {})`; Google switches method and builds query via URLSearchParams:
     ```ts
     const method = stream ? "streamGenerateContent" : "generateContent";
     const params = new URLSearchParams();
     if (stream) params.set("alt", "sse");
     if (apiKey) params.set("key", apiKey);
     const query = params.toString();
     url: `${withoutTrailingSlash(settings.baseUrl)}/models/${encodedModel}:${method}${query ? `?${query}` : ""}`
     ```
     - New chunk-boundary-safe SSE parser:
     ```ts
     const EVENT_SEPARATOR = /\r?\n\r?\n/;

     export function createSseParser(): (chunk: string) => string[] {
       let buffer = "";
       return (chunk: string) => {
         buffer += chunk;
         const events: string[] = [];
         for (let match = EVENT_SEPARATOR.exec(buffer); match; match = EVENT_SEPARATOR.exec(buffer)) {
           const rawEvent = buffer.slice(0, match.index);
           buffer = buffer.slice(match.index + match[0].length);
           const data = rawEvent
             .split(/\r?\n/)
             .filter((line) => line.startsWith("data:"))
             .map((line) => line.slice(5).trim())
             .join("\n");
           if (data) events.push(data);
         }
         return events;
       };
     }
     ```
     - Per-provider delta extraction, throwing on mid-stream provider errors:
     ```ts
     export function extractStreamDelta(settings: ProviderSettings, data: string): string {
       if (!data || data === "[DONE]") return "";
       let payload: any;
       try { payload = JSON.parse(data); } catch { return ""; }
       if (payload?.error) {
         throw new Error(providerErrorMessage(payload, "The provider reported a streaming error."));
       }
       if (settings.provider === "anthropic") {
         if (payload.type === "content_block_delta" && payload.delta?.type === "text_delta") {
           return typeof payload.delta.text === "string" ? payload.delta.text : "";
         }
         return "";
       }
       if (settings.provider === "google") {
         return textFromParts(payload?.candidates?.[0]?.content?.parts);
       }
       const delta = payload?.choices?.[0]?.delta;
       if (typeof delta?.content === "string") return delta.content;
       return textFromParts(delta?.content);
     }
     ```
     - `streamCompletion` with the content-based (not body-null-based) fallback:
     ```ts
     export interface StreamCompletionOptions extends ProviderRequestOptions {
       onDelta?: (delta: string, accumulated: string) => void;
       fetchImpl?: FetchLike;
     }

     export async function streamCompletion(settings, apiKey, messages, options: StreamCompletionOptions = {}): Promise<string> {
       const { onDelta, fetchImpl = fetch, ...requestOptions } = options;
       const request = buildProviderRequest(settings, apiKey, messages, { ...requestOptions, stream: true });
       const response = await fetchImpl(request.url, request.init);
       if (!response.ok) await throwProviderError(response);

       const body = response.body;
       if (!body) {
         // No readable stream on this platform — take the whole payload at once.
         return wholePayloadFallback(settings, await response.text(), onDelta);
       }

       const decoder = new TextDecoder();
       const parse = createSseParser();
       const reader = body.getReader();
       let accumulated = "";
       let raw = "";
       try {
         while (true) {
           const { done, value } = await reader.read();
           if (done) break;
           const chunk = decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });
           raw += chunk;
           for (const data of parse(chunk)) {
             const delta = extractStreamDelta(settings, data);
             if (!delta) continue;
             accumulated += delta;
             onDelta?.(delta, accumulated);
           }
         }
       } finally {
         reader.releaseLock();
       }

       const trimmed = accumulated.trim();
       if (trimmed) return trimmed;
       // Some OpenAI-compatible servers (local runtimes especially) ignore
       // `stream: true` and answer with one plain JSON body instead of SSE.
       return wholePayloadFallback(settings, raw, onDelta);
     }

     function wholePayloadFallback(settings, text, onDelta?): string {
       let payload: unknown;
       try { payload = text.trim() ? JSON.parse(text) : {}; }
       catch { throw new Error("The provider returned a response without readable text."); }
       const content = extractProviderText(settings, payload);
       onDelta?.(content, content);
       return content;
     }
